# Source location: https://github.com/MelkhiorVintageComputing/RD68041
#
# Where QEMU's m68040 (B) and UAE040 (A) part on tools/cosim/uae040/tests/
# smoke040.S, each confirmed on every `make cosim-qemu-smoke`
# (tools/cosim/qemu040/compare.py --expect). One "<label> <field>" a line,
# shell patterns; doc/oracles.md ("QEMU") has the evidence and which of the
# two the manual supports.
#
# Reset: FP0-FP7 are NaN in QEMU, zero in UAE040. UM 8.2.10 does not say.
_start          fp[0-7][ehl]
# MOVEC of all ones to ITT0 and TC reads back all ones in QEMU: it does not
# clear the reserved bits (UM 3.1.2, 3.1.3; UAE040 does).
L_int+1a        d5
L_int+2e        d6
# Access error frame (format $7): QEMU stacks the fault address in the
# effective address field at +$08, UAE040 0 (UM 8.4.6.1).
aerr+10         a3
# PTESTW: QEMU's MMUSR has no M (UM 3.1.4: a write search sets it; UAE040 does).
L_ptest         d4
# A DTTR over $00xxxxxx with S ignored: QEMU still translates through the tables
# (reads PA $30000, not $20000).
L_pflush+10     d4
L_pflush+10     sr
# No data cache in QEMU: CINVA cannot lose the dirty line.
L_cb3           d2
L_cb3           sr
# FSIN: QEMU executes it, the MC68040 does not implement it (UM table 9-10:
# vector 11, format $2; UAE040 traps), and what follows differs with it.
fline           pc
L_fsin          *
